1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:12,160
-ss 5 and -to 10: how long is the clip?

2
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:16,780
One source, five cuts.

3
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:24,040
500 unique frames, lossless.

4
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:34,920
Readers: ffprobe, and frame md5 match.

5
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:43,890
-ss 5 -to 10 -i: 5 s, source 5 to 10.

6
00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:47,960
Both after -i: the same.

7
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:59,200
-ss 5 -i ... -to 10: 10 s, source 5 to 15.

8
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,820
-to counts on the new clock.

9
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:14,010
-ss 5 -i ... -t 5: 5 s, source 5 to 10.

10
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:20,140
-to 10 -i alone: the first 10 s.

11
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:27,720
Keep -ss and -to together, or use -t.

12
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:33,400
Check the duration of every cut.
